# HiFadithi: the 3D pipeline end to end (steps 1-5 of docs/e2e-script.md). Owner: C.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP client.
# Fill in the variables; never commit real passwords or tokens.

@host = https://hifadithi-api.onrender.com
@username = researcher-username
@password = researcher-password

### 1. Sign in as a researcher (copy "access" into @access below)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/token/
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "{{username}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

###
@access = paste-access-token-here

### 2. Create an artefact (copy "id" into @artefact)
POST {{host}}/api/artefacts/
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nmk_accession_no": "TEST-001", "title": "Test object", "community": "Turkana",
 "object_type": "Headdress", "height_mm": 300, "width_mm": 250, "depth_mm": 120}

###
@artefact = paste-artefact-id-here

### 3a. Start a capture: returns the capture "id" and 4 upload links (1 hour, JPEG only)
POST {{host}}/api/artefacts/{{artefact}}/captures/
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

###
@capture = paste-capture-id-here
@upload_front = paste-upload_urls.front-here

### 3b. Upload each photo with its own link (repeat for back, left, right).
# Must send exactly Content-Type: image/jpeg. Use test photos only, never NMK photos here.
PUT {{upload_front}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./front.jpg

### 3c. Mark the capture complete (400 missing_views if a photo is missing)
POST {{host}}/api/artefacts/captures/{{capture}}/complete/
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

### 4. Start the 3D job (copy "id" into @job)
POST {{host}}/api/jobs/
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"capture_id": "{{capture}}"}

###
@job = paste-job-id-here

### 5. Check the job: repeat until "status" is "succeeded" (review_status needs_verification)
GET {{host}}/api/jobs/{{job}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

### The model then shows in Admin → Pipeline → Jobs → this job.
